From: genetixteam <genetixteam@gmail.com>
Subject: fw4: keep the bridge device in the hw offload flowtable

With hardware offload fw4 replaces br-lan with its member ports. Wi-Fi
flows cannot resolve a forward path through mac80211, so the kernel keeps
br-lan as their ingress device; with br-lan missing from the flowtable,
every packet from a Wi-Fi client took the full slow path (EX20v v2:
Wi-Fi 130 Mbit/s with hw offload vs 280 with software offload). Keep the
bridge itself next to its lower devices.

diff --git a/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc b/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
index 617d8a5..4e2c0a8 100644
--- a/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
@@ -447,7 +447,16 @@ function resolve_lower_devices(devstatus, devname) {
 	let devs = [];
 
 	if (dir) {
-		switch (devstatus[devname]?.devtype ?? sysfs_devtype(devname)) {
+		let dt = devstatus[devname]?.devtype ?? sysfs_devtype(devname);
+
+		/* EX20v: keep the bridge itself too. Wi-Fi flows cannot resolve a
+		 * forward path through mac80211, so their tuples keep br-lan as
+		 * the ingress device; without br-lan in the flowtable those
+		 * packets never reach the software fast path. */
+		if (dt == 'bridge')
+			push(devs, devname);
+
+		switch (dt) {
 		case 'vlan':
 		case 'bridge':
 			let e;
